  - ci/image/command-table.json: names submodule source(s) literally that are not permitted prose: protocol-processor/hdl/acmp/KL_acmp_nvm_shadow.sv, protocol-processor/hdl/acmp/pp_acmp_pkg.sv, protocol-processor/hdl/adp/pp_adp_pkg.sv, protocol-processor/hdl/aecp/KL_aecp_dyn_state.sv, protocol-processor/hdl/packet_engine/KL_pp_nvm_mgr_arb.sv, protocol-processor/hdl/packet_engine/KL_pp_nvm_port.sv. A build input must derive the list with this script. If this really is prose, add the exact literal to PROSE_OK with the reason.

A build input names a stale set of submodule sources. This is what a
submodule bump breaks and what nothing used to catch: the copies are
correct against the pin they were written for and go stale the moment it
moves. Derive the list with this script rather than editing the copy.
